{
  "case_id": "2008-07-1372",
  "document_hash": "7b71e5e2d8beed064dde295e1418f6a4a12534de208094bed020f7c713ac85a2",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Gen. Mark J. Bennett",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1372",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b71e5e2d8beed064dde295e1418f6a4a12534de208094bed020f7c713ac85a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b71e5e2d8be-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A 1993 congressional apology resolution did not alter Hawaii's right to transfer its public lands or repeal, by implication, prior congressional enactments that it extinguish all competing claims to those lands. It was, as its sponsor said at the time, a simple apology, and no more."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1372",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b71e5e2d8beed064dde295e1418f6a4a12534de208094bed020f7c713ac85a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b71e5e2d8be-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Excuse me. Does that proposition settle the question whether your opponents have equitable interest in the lands?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Gen. Mark J. Bennett",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1372",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b71e5e2d8beed064dde295e1418f6a4a12534de208094bed020f7c713ac85a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b71e5e2d8be-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, what the Respondents have contended from day one in this case is that they have a property right in this -- in the land, and the Newlands Resolution conclusively settled that question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1372",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b71e5e2d8beed064dde295e1418f6a4a12534de208094bed020f7c713ac85a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b71e5e2d8be-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Why is it necessary? Why isn't it sufficient just to say that this resolution has no substantive effect, period, and then remand to the Hawaii Supreme Court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1372",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b71e5e2d8beed064dde295e1418f6a4a12534de208094bed020f7c713ac85a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b71e5e2d8be-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Is -- is it the function of the Hawaiian Supreme Court to declare moral obligations?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1372",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b71e5e2d8beed064dde295e1418f6a4a12534de208094bed020f7c713ac85a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b71e5e2d8be-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. JAY: The legislature could determine that the wisest use of the lands today, the way that would best further -- promote the welfare of Native Hawaiians today would be not to sell it. The legislature certainly could do that and then could enact a moratorium that was consistent with that view."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kannon K. Shanmugam",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1372",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b71e5e2d8beed064dde295e1418f6a4a12534de208094bed020f7c713ac85a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b71e5e2d8be-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SHANMUGAM: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The only issue properly presented in this case is whether the Hawaii Supreme Court concluded that the Apology Resolution created an affirmative federal obligation not to sell ceded land. In our view, it did not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1372",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b71e5e2d8beed064dde295e1418f6a4a12534de208094bed020f7c713ac85a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b71e5e2d8be-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: You don't?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1372",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b71e5e2d8beed064dde295e1418f6a4a12534de208094bed020f7c713ac85a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b71e5e2d8be-0002-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "presumably, according to the terms of the injunction, it would no longer have any force."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1372",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b71e5e2d8beed064dde295e1418f6a4a12534de208094bed020f7c713ac85a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b71e5e2d8be-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would note, however, parenthetically, that immediately after this litigation was commenced the Hawaii Department of Land and Natural Resources imposed a unilateral moratorium on the sale of ceded lands."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1372",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b71e5e2d8beed064dde295e1418f6a4a12534de208094bed020f7c713ac85a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b71e5e2d8be-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is undisputed that Respondents asserted a property-interest claim. That any property-interest claim is, in fact, inconsistent with Federal law. That the State has perfect title to these lands, and that there is no possible reason why this Court should not disabuse the State court of the incorrect notion that the State lacks perfect title."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1372",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7b71e5e2d8beed064dde295e1418f6a4a12534de208094bed020f7c713ac85a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b71e5e2d8be-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "and there is no reason why in this 14-year-old litigation this Court should not make clear the simple and indisputed fact that, pursuant to the Newlands Resolution, the Organic Act and the Admission Act, that the State has perfect title."
    },
    {
